From: Michael Narine <michael@verita-ai.com>
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 17:17:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Print: initialise m_isBBLPrinter to false

Print::m_isBBLPrinter is never initialised in Print's constructor or in its
declaration. Orca's own CLI and GUI always assign it after constructing a Print, so
the bug is hidden there, but any other caller reads an indeterminate value. In the
wild this flips G-code generation to the Bambu dialect ("; FEATURE:" comments,
M486, M981) depending on heap contents.

Value-initialise it to false at its declaration.

Purpose: Fix an uninitialised member: Print::m_isBBLPrinter can flip G-code to the Bambu dialect depending on heap contents.
SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
Upstream-Status: to be submitted
Orca-Base: v2.4.2
---
diff --git a/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp b/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
--- a/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
@@ -1154,7 +1154,7 @@
     PrintRegionPtrs                         m_print_regions;
     
     //SoftFever
-    bool m_isBBLPrinter;
+    bool m_isBBLPrinter = false;
 
     // Ordered collections of extrusion paths to build skirt loops and brim.
     ExtrusionEntityCollection               m_skirt;
